# 30-Day Gut Health Reset Meal Plan for Women 45+
## The Estrobolome Protocol

### What This Is
A 30-day meal plan designed to support the gut-hormone connection (estrobolome) for women going through perimenopause and menopause. Each day includes 3 meals + 2 snacks, all focused on high-fiber whole foods that feed beneficial gut bacteria and help regulate estrogen metabolism.

### Daily Targets
- Fiber: 30-35g
- Water: 2-2.5L
- Fermented foods: 1 serving/day
- Omega-3: 2 servings/week

### Week 1: Foundation
**Day 1**
- Breakfast: Overnight oats (80g oats + 250ml almond milk + 1 tbsp chia seeds + 1/2 cup blueberries)
- Lunch: Quinoa bowl with roasted chickpeas, spinach, avocado, lemon-tahini dressing
- Dinner: Baked salmon (150g) + steamed broccoli (200g) + sweet potato (150g)
- Snacks: 1 apple + 30g walnuts; 1 cup kefir

**Day 2**
- Breakfast: Smoothie (1 banana + 1 cup spinach + 1 tbsp flaxseed + 250ml kefir + 1/2 cup frozen berries)
- Lunch: Lentil soup (500ml) + side salad with olive oil
- Dinner: Chicken stir-fry (150g chicken) with bok choy, bell peppers, ginger, served over brown rice
- Snacks: Hummus (3 tbsp) + carrots; 1 pear

**Day 3**
- Breakfast: Scrambled eggs (2) + sauerkraut (2 tbsp) + sourdough toast (1 slice)
- Lunch: Stuffed bell peppers with black beans, brown rice, salsa
- Dinner: Sardines (1 tin) + roasted vegetables (zucchini, eggplant, onion) + quinoa
- Snacks: 1 orange + 30g almonds; 1 cup kimchi

(Days 4-30 follow same pattern — full 30-day version available in premium PDF)

### Foods to Prioritize
- Soluble fiber: oats, beans, lentils, apples, flaxseed
- Fermented foods: kefir, kimchi, sauerkraut, miso
- Cruciferous vegetables: broccoli, cauliflower, Brussels sprouts
- Omega-3: salmon, sardines, walnuts, flaxseed

### Foods to Limit
- Alcohol, refined sugar, processed seed oils, artificial sweeteners

### Important Notes
- This is a nutritional guide, not medical advice. Consult your doctor before making dietary changes.
- Individual results vary. Track how you feel at week 2 and week 4.

